SM-T715 tablet: the SD card tile, over t715-sdcard.

The microSD slot's own tile: on while the card is mounted, off with a card in
but not mounted (a tap mounts it, about a second) or with no card. The
session's udiskie already mounts a card that goes in, so the tile shows and
changes the state rather than owning it. A long press opens the card in
Files (Disks when it cannot be read). Without the command or the slot no
sdcard key is probed and the tile stays dimmed, so an image without
t715-sdcard or a kernel without the slot never fails. The SM-T715's 0.2.94
series' 0012-tablet-sdcard-tile, rebased. Against omarchy-mobile 8991845
(omamobile-shell 0.2.147), after 0001-0008.

